description.en:
The structure of ECOICOP-HICP is limited to the  ECOICOP codes actually used in the HICP (Harmonised Index of Consumer Prices). 
The ECOICOP codes (and their sub-items) not used for HICP purposes are the following: 
02.3 – Narcotics; 
04.2 – Imputed rentals for housing; 
09.4.3 – Games of chance; 
12.2 – Prostitution; 
12.5.1 – Life insurance; 
12.6.1 – FISIM. 
To facilitate further analysis of consumer price developments, over 30 special aggregates  (groups of individual ECOICOPs) are available as Collection, such as Food, Services, Energy, Non-energy industrial goods, etc.
